ue, "input_schema": {"properties": {"display_name": {"description": "Optional short label to prefill in the form, e.g. \"Example API token\"; it names the credential in the environment's network secrets list. The user can change it. Plain text only: no URLs, links or markup.", "type": "string"}, "header_name": {"description": "Optional. The HTTP header the API reads the key from, e.g. \"xi-api-key\" or \"X-Api-Key\". Send it only when the user or the API's documentation says the key goes in a header other than Authorization: Bearer; leave it out otherwise. One word of letters, digits, hyphens and underscores: at most 40 characters, in at most 5 hyphen-separated parts of at most 16 characters each, and the last part must be key, apikey, token, auth, authorization, secret, credential or credentials. The form cannot save a key under any other header: for an API that reads one, the user adds the key in the environment's settings. Prefills the form; the user can change it. Not used with suggested_type \"basic\". Never put a key's value in this or any other field.", "type": "string"}, "host": {"description": "The exact hostname the credential is for, e.g. \"api.example.com\". Lowercase DNS name only — no scheme, path, port, IP address or wildcard. Shown to the user in the form.", "type": "string"}, "prefix": {"description": "Optional. The word the API expects before the key in the header: one of Bearer, Token, Key, ApiKey, Api-Key, Bot, SSWS, Splunk or GenieKey, in any letter case. With the Authorization header it defaults to Bearer; with any other header_name it defaults to none, so pass prefix whenever the documentation shows a word before the key, Bearer included. The form cannot save a key with any other word before it: for an API that expects one, the user adds the key in the environment's settings. Not used with suggested_type \"basic\". Never put a key's value in this or any other field.", "type": "string"}, "reason": {"description": "One or two sentences: which re